## Edge Cases

| # | Feature | Input | Observed Behavior |
|---|---------|-------|-------------------|
| 1 | Txt Header | Slice length $< 100$ bytes | Returns `Err(FlightReaderError::UnexpectedEof { needed: 100, ... })` without panicking |
| 2 | Txt Header | Header length field indicates 101 bytes, but input buffer is exactly 100 bytes | Returns `Err(FlightReaderError::UnexpectedEof { needed: 101, ... })` |
| 3 | Txt Header | Header length field is neither 100 nor 101 (e.g. 99, 102, 0) | Returns `Err(FlightReaderError::InvalidHeaderLength { length })` |
| 4 | Txt Header | Version byte is 0 or $> 14$ (e.g. 255) | Returns `Err(FlightReaderError::UnsupportedVersion { version })` |
| 5 | Txt Header | ScrambledFlag is 0 (v1–v6 legacy plaintext) | Sets `scrambled_flag = 0`; indicates record payloads must bypass XOR de-scrambling |
| 6 | Crypto XOR | Payload slice with length 0 or 1 byte (missing payload body) | Returns `Err(FlightReaderError::PayloadTooShort { minimum: 2, actual })` |
| 7 | Crypto XOR | Seed is 0 (`data[0] == 0x00`) | Multiplier product $1311768467463790320 \times 0 = 0$; `mem = [0; 8]`; CRC initial accumulator becomes `record_type % 256`; produces deterministic non-zero keystream |
| 8 | Crypto XOR | Degenerate seeds (multiples of 15: 0, 15, 30, ... 225) | Product collapses to repetitive byte lanes ($P$ has $\le 2$ unique bytes), but combination with `crc_0` and reflected CRC64 yields 0% keystream collisions across all 14,592 test pairs |
| 9 | Crypto XOR | In-place de-scrambling buffer with odd length (e.g. 13 bytes) | Cyclic mask wraps smoothly using `i % 8`; trailing 5 bytes correctly mask against key bytes 0..4 |
| 10 | Crypto XOR | Destination slice capacity in `descramble_slice` is smaller than source slice | Returns `Err(FlightReaderError::BufferOverflow)` immediately before mutating destination |
| 11 | DAT Framing | Stream containing random noise bytes before magic byte `0x55` | Iterator skips noise bytes one-by-one until `0x55` is encountered; parses frame cleanly |
| 12 | DAT Framing | Byte `0x55` followed by invalid length field $< 11$ (e.g. 0, 5, 10) | Rejects candidate as stream noise; advances cursor by 1 byte to resume search |
| 13 | DAT Framing | Valid header but corrupted payload triggering CRC16 mismatch | Emits `Err(FlightReaderError::ChecksumMismatch)`; advances cursor by 1 to re-synchronize |
| 14 | DAT Framing | Zero-length payload frame ($\text{Length} = 11$ with CRC16, or $13$ with CRC32) | Yields valid `DatFrame` with empty payload slice `&[]`; verified against checksum |
| 15 | DAT Framing | Truncated frame at end of stream ($\text{cursor} + \text{Length} > \text{stream.len()}$) | Halts iteration and returns `None` without panic or out-of-bounds index errors |
| 16 | DAT Checksum | Frame with alternating polynomial noise resembling CRC16 | CRC16 verification fails ($p = 1 - 2^{-16} \approx 99.9985\%$ rejection rate); stream parser continues |

